{"content_hash": "f786e5520f9724fe", "version_id": 694, "article_id": 70, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "France arrests 1,200 as protests turn violent", "title_zh": "法国抗议失控，1200多人被捕", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6d937wedj7jo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1485504750689-aa2121ffe6c6?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8dmlvbGVudCUyMGNsYXNoZXMlMjBsb290aW5nfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTIyNzkxMjd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Pawel Janiak on Unsplash", "author": "Pawel Janiak", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@pawelj?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/fire-burning-on-the-road-with-high-rise-buildings-during-daytime-photography-49LBMXrY5BE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(36, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(74, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "f2043e6acb50"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-18", "word_count": 239, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "Violence spread across France on Saturday as hundreds of thousands of people protested against the cost of living and poor conditions in schools. The government said more than 1,200 people were arrested.", "lead_zh": "周六，数十万法国人因生活成本上涨和学校条件恶劣走上街头抗议，暴力事件在全国蔓延。政府表示，已有超过1200人被捕。", "preview": "An estimated 550,000 people took to the streets on Saturday, according to the French government. In Paris, the main march was mostly peacefu", "preview_zh": "据法国政府估计，周六约有55万人走上街头。在巴黎，下午的主要游行基本和平，但傍晚与防暴警察发生了冲突。警察对人群使用了催泪瓦斯和高压水枪，有人看到防暴警察冲撞人群并用警棍打人。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 682, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 91.0, "size_bytes": 546912, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 279, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 92.75, "size_bytes": 557424, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 279, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/70/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 98.975, "size_bytes": 594864, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 279, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/70/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 85.075, "size_bytes": 511344, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 279, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/70/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/70/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 92.3, "size_bytes": 554688, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 279, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/70/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fec3522/content/data/versions/694.json", "paragraphs": ["An estimated 550,000 people took to the streets on Saturday, according to the French government. In Paris, the main march was mostly peaceful during the afternoon, but clashes with riot police broke out later in the evening. Officers used tear gas and water cannon against crowds, and riot police were seen charging at people and hitting them with batons.", "Buildings were set on fire in several cities. In Limoges, a large fire at the town hall caused part of the roof to collapse. In Lyon, the city's tourist office burned down, which Mayor Grégory Doucet called \"a tragedy\" for the city. Shops were also ransacked, including an Apple store in Lille that was emptied.", "Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said 150 police officers were injured and that some groups were using the protests as a \"warm-up\" for next year's presidential election. President Emmanuel Macron warned that those who attacked buildings and looted shops would be prosecuted and punished.", "The protests began with students angry about staff shortages and run-down schools, and were later joined by trade unions and the \"yellow vest\" movement. The unrest comes as France faces deep political uncertainty, with Macron leaving office next year and the presidential election expected to be closely contested.", "Jean-Luc Mélenchon of the hard-left party took part in the demonstrations and accused the police of \"unleashing\" on protesters, while Marine Le Pen said the far left had taken the protesters' \"legitimate demands\" hostage."], "paragraphs_zh": ["据法国政府估计，周六约有55万人走上街头。在巴黎，下午的主要游行基本和平，但傍晚与防暴警察发生了冲突。警察对人群使用了催泪瓦斯和高压水枪，有人看到防暴警察冲撞人群并用警棍打人。", "多座城市的建筑被纵火。在利摩日，市政厅燃起大火，导致部分屋顶坍塌。在里昂，市旅游办公室被烧毁，市长格雷戈里·杜塞称这对该市来说是“一场悲剧”。商店也遭到洗劫，包括里尔一家被搬空的苹果商店。", "总理塞巴斯蒂安·勒科尔尼表示，150名警察受伤，一些团体把抗议当作明年总统选举的“热身”。总统埃马纽埃尔·马克龙警告说，袭击建筑和抢劫商店的人将被起诉并受到惩罚。", "抗议最初由学生对师资短缺和校舍破旧的不满引发，后来工会和“黄背心”运动也加入其中。这场骚乱发生之际，法国正面临深刻的政治不确定性，马克龙将于明年卸任，总统选举预计将竞争激烈。", "极左翼政党人物让-吕克·梅朗雄参加了示威，并指责警察对示威者“放手施暴”；玛丽娜·勒庞则表示，极左翼把抗议者的“合理诉求”当成了人质。"], "body": "An estimated 550,000 people took to the streets on Saturday, according to the French government. In Paris, the main march was mostly peaceful during the afternoon, but clashes with riot police broke out later in the evening. Officers used tear gas and water cannon against crowds, and riot police were seen charging at people and hitting them with batons.\n\nBuildings were set on fire in several cities. In Limoges, a large fire at the town hall caused part of the roof to collapse. In Lyon, the city's tourist office burned down, which Mayor Grégory Doucet called \"a tragedy\" for the city. Shops were also ransacked, including an Apple store in Lille that was emptied.\n\nPrime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said 150 police officers were injured and that some groups were using the protests as a \"warm-up\" for next year's presidential election. President Emmanuel Macron warned that those who attacked buildings and looted shops would be prosecuted and punished.\n\nThe protests began with students angry about staff shortages and run-down schools, and were later joined by trade unions and the \"yellow vest\" movement. The unrest comes as France faces deep political uncertainty, with Macron leaving office next year and the presidential election expected to be closely contested.\n\nJean-Luc Mélenchon of the hard-left party took part in the demonstrations and accused the police of \"unleashing\" on protesters, while Marine Le Pen said the far left had taken the protesters' \"legitimate demands\" hostage.", "body_zh": "据法国政府估计，周六约有55万人走上街头。在巴黎，下午的主要游行基本和平，但傍晚与防暴警察发生了冲突。警察对人群使用了催泪瓦斯和高压水枪，有人看到防暴警察冲撞人群并用警棍打人。\n\n多座城市的建筑被纵火。在利摩日，市政厅燃起大火，导致部分屋顶坍塌。在里昂，市旅游办公室被烧毁，市长格雷戈里·杜塞称这对该市来说是“一场悲剧”。商店也遭到洗劫，包括里尔一家被搬空的苹果商店。\n\n总理塞巴斯蒂安·勒科尔尼表示，150名警察受伤，一些团体把抗议当作明年总统选举的“热身”。总统埃马纽埃尔·马克龙警告说，袭击建筑和抢劫商店的人将被起诉并受到惩罚。\n\n抗议最初由学生对师资短缺和校舍破旧的不满引发，后来工会和“黄背心”运动也加入其中。这场骚乱发生之际，法国正面临深刻的政治不确定性，马克龙将于明年卸任，总统选举预计将竞争激烈。\n\n极左翼政党人物让-吕克·梅朗雄参加了示威，并指责警察对示威者“放手施暴”；玛丽娜·勒庞则表示，极左翼把抗议者的“合理诉求”当成了人质。", "text": "An estimated 550,000 people took to the streets on Saturday, according to the French government. In Paris, the main march was mostly peaceful during the afternoon, but clashes with riot police broke out later in the evening. Officers used tear gas and water cannon against crowds, and riot police were seen charging at people and hitting them with batons. Buildings were set on fire in several cities. In Limoges, a large fire at the town hall caused part of the roof to collapse. In Lyon, the city's tourist office burned down, which Mayor Grégory Doucet called \"a tragedy\" for the city. Shops were also ransacked, including an Apple store in Lille that was emptied. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said 150 police officers were injured and that some groups were using the protests as a \"warm-up\" for next year's presidential election. President Emmanuel Macron warned that those who attacked buildings and looted shops would be prosecuted and punished. The protests began with students angry about staff shortages and run-down schools, and were later joined by trade unions and the \"yellow vest\" movement. The unrest comes as France faces deep political uncertainty, with Macron leaving office next year and the presidential election expected to be closely contested. Jean-Luc Mélenchon of the hard-left party took part in the demonstrations and accused the police of \"unleashing\" on protesters, while Marine Le Pen said the far left had taken the protesters' \"legitimate demands\" hostage.", "vocab": [{"word": "clash", "pos": "noun", "zh": "冲突", "note": "常指人群或警察之间的暴力冲突", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "looting", "pos": "noun", "zh": "抢劫；洗劫", "note": "常指骚乱中趁乱抢劫商店", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "ablaze", "pos": "adj", "zh": "着火的", "note": "常见搭配 be ablaze / set ablaze", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "tear gas", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "催泪瓦斯", "note": "警察驱散人群时使用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "water cannon", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "高压水枪", "note": "常用于控制人群", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "vandalism", "pos": "noun", "zh": "故意破坏公物", "note": "指破坏公共或他人财产的行为", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "ransack", "pos": "verb", "zh": "洗劫；翻得乱七八糟", "note": "比 rob 更强调把地方翻乱", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "prosecute", "pos": "verb", "zh": "起诉", "note": "法律用语，指正式起诉某人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "unrest", "pos": "noun", "zh": "动荡；骚乱", "note": "不可数名词，常指社会或政治不安", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "demonstration", "pos": "noun", "zh": "示威游行", "note": "比 protest 更正式", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "legitimate", "pos": "a